{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallest","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Eigenpairs","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryFloatingPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SB"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"smallest","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The number of eigenpairs, in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"weight","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The weight of the edge at each position."}]}]},{"name":"tolerance","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The residual a Ritz pair must reach, relative as described above.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"maxIterations","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under Throws."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"text":" · λ, relative to itself as for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"algebraicConnectivity"},{"text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"smallest","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", every weight is finite"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and nonnegative, and "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" products","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"20√n products or ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"laplacianSpectrum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The k smallest eigenvalues of the normalized Laplacian N (","type":"text"},{"code":"normalizedLaplacianMatrix()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"= ","type":"text"},{"code":"smallest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ascending, each with a unit eigenvector (see ","type":"text"},{"code":"Eigenpairs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/normalizedlaplacianeigenpairs(smallest:weight:tolerance:maxiterations:)-2kxtv"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs(smallest:weight:tolerance:maxIterations:)-2kxtv"},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method"